---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLine from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout sideBarActiveItemID="journey" title="Journey | Agueda Schwartz" description="From education research in Lima to building 0-to-1 AI products in the US. Career timeline, education, and certifications.">
  <div class="pb-8 mt-5">
    <div class="text-lg opacity-75">
      From education research in Lima to building 0-to-1 AI products in the US. Here's how I got here.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Experience</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="Product Manager, WGU Labs"
      subtitle="Sep 2022 to Present | Remote"
    >
      Took a stalled AI Entrepreneurship Portfolio through discovery, market validation, evidence-based pivot, and a 12-week learning pilot with seven committed early adopters. Designed a four-phase innovation framework (Sense → Shape → Test → Scale) to structure my own work, applied it honestly, and course-corrected when it showed I'd over-invested in research. Built an operating model on Claude Code to run the full product cycle solo. Facilitated a cross-functional AI upskilling workshop.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Senior to Lead Learning Experience Designer, WGU Labs"
      subtitle="Jun 2021 to Sep 2022 | Remote"
    >
      Designed a multi-month train-of-trainers workshop series for ~40 nursing faculty at a major public research university transitioning the BA and MA programs to competency-based education. Redesigned online learning modules and contributed to curriculum development across partner engagements. Promoted from Senior to Lead in 15 months.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Learning and Development Specialist, Berdon LLP"
      subtitle="Jun 2020 to Jun 2021 | New York, NY"
    >
      Contributed to the internal learning platform for senior accountants, partners, and tax attorneys at an NYC accounting firm. Owned the annual content refresh across 200+ modules covering tax policy, professional education, and compliance training. Stood up LinkedIn Learning as a supplementary content channel, and contributed to a firm-wide CPE compliance tracker that confirmed license renewals across LinkedIn Learning, external courses, and internal training. Led the firm's adoption of Human Centered Design with backing from the Director of L&D, building a community that drove cross-functional connection across the firm.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Product Owner, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Nov 2017 to Jul 2018 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Owned the full lifecycle of an enterprise assessment platform deployed to 2,000 users across 20+ school locations. Drove a 30% reduction in data input errors across 30,000 transactions and a 10% reduction in user task time, both measured at the end of the first cycle. Talked to users continuously through deployment and facilitated train-of-trainers sessions on the Innovation department's methodology.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Monitoring and Evaluation Manager, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Mar 2016 to Oct 2017 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Designed evaluations centered on learning outcomes for 4 platform pilots across 20+ school locations, including Khan Academy, an ESL platform, and a leadership and collaboration skills program. Research recommendations were the primary evidence leadership used to drive network-wide adoption and sunset decisions. Contributed to a multidisciplinary effort shaping a competency framework for teacher development.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Monitoring and Evaluation Coordinator, Innova Schools"
      subtitle="Mar 2014 to Feb 2016 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Contributed to building an evaluation methodology with a small team for assessing innovation pilots, with learning outcomes as the primary criterion. The methodology became the starting point for the platform evaluations I would later own as Manager. Coordinated a team of data collectors in the field and led the qualitative research myself: observations, interviews, and focus groups.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Research Assistant, Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú"
      subtitle="Jul 2010 to Feb 2014 | Lima, Peru"
    >
      Conducted research on educational technology and digital learning resources.
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Education</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="MA, Digital Media Design for Learning"
      subtitle="New York University | 2018 to 2020"
    >
      Digital media, instructional design, and learning science.
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="BA, Educational Psychology"
      subtitle="Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú | 2005 to 2012"
    >
      Learning theory, cognitive science, and research methodology. The foundation for everything I build.
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Certifications</div>

    <TimeLine
      title="Designing Strategy"
      subtitle="IDEO U | 2024"
    >
    </TimeLine>

    <TimeLine
      title="Designing a Business"
      subtitle="IDEO U | 2023"
    >
    </TimeLine>
  </div>

</BaseLayout>
